  "query_preview": "/Thursday through Monday/...\nIssued 126 AM MDT MON OCT 26 2026\nIncreasing southwesterly flow on Thursday will allow for another few \ndegrees of warmup, with dry conditions as brief shortwave ridging \nbuilds in ahead of the next system. Guidance seems to be backing off \nof the southern split solution mentioned in last nights discussion \n(if you read that one :) ), with ensembles now favoring a more \nnorthern track. With this, the best chances of precipitation will \ncome over the weekend in southwest Idaho, after increasing late \nFriday in the Central Idaho Mountains. Snow levels for this system \nwill range from 4-6kft MSL, increasing from west to east.\nTemperatures will continue to be seasonable for the time of year \nthrough the period.",
